{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"414","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Mashmokh's Designed Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After a lot of trying, Mashmokh designed a problem and it's your job to solve it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have a tree "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices. Each vertex has a unique index from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". The root of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" has index "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". For each vertex of this tree "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":", you are given a list of its children in a specific order. You must perform three types of query on this tree:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" find distance (the number of edges in the shortest path) between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" given "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":", disconnect "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" from its father and connect it to its "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th ancestor; more formally, let's denote the path from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the root by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, x2, ..., xl (h < l)"},{"kind":"text","text":", so that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1 = v"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xl"},{"kind":"text","text":" is root; disconnect "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" from its father ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"text","text":") and connect it to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xh + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"; vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be added to the end of the child-list of vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xh + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the vertex sequence produced by calling function dfs(root) find the latest vertex that has distance "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the root. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The pseudo-code of function dfs(v): "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n// ls[v]: list of children of vertex v \n// its i-th element is ls[v][i]\n// its size is size(ls[v])\nsequence result = empty sequence;\nvoid dfs(vertex now)\n{\n    add now to end of result;\n    for(int i = 1; i <= size(ls[v]); i = i + 1) //loop from i = 1 to i = size(ls[v])\n        dfs(ls[v][i]);\n}\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains two space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m (2 ≤ n ≤ 105; 1 ≤ m ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":", the number of vertices of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" and number of queries to perform."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li (0 ≤ li ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":", number of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th vertex's children. Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated integers follow, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them is the index of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th child of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th vertex. Note that the order of these vertices is important."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines has one of the following format: \""},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", or \""},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". The first number in the line is the type of query to perform according to the problem statement. The next numbers are description of the query."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that all the queries are correct. For example, in the second-type query "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" is at least 2 and at most distance of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" from root. Also in the third-type query there is at least one vertex with distance "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the root at the time the query is given."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query of the first or third type output one line containing the result of the query."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 9\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n0\n1 1 4\n2 4 2\n1 3 4\n3 1\n3 2\n2 3 2\n1 1 2\n3 1\n3 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n2\n2\n4\n1\n3\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2\n1 2\n0\n1 2 1\n3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"414E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/414/problem/E"}